# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  CLARA — deny by default, allow only source.
#
#  This folder is ~90,000 files: model weights, a vendored Python,
#  llama.cpp binaries, Docker volumes and n8n data. Almost none of
#  it belongs on GitHub, and some of it is private.
#
#  So: ignore everything at the root, then re-admit the handful of
#  directories that are actually source. Anything new you drop in
#  the root is ignored until you deliberately allow it here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

/*


# ─── Source: the only things that get committed ────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/LICENSE
!/CLARA.cmd
!/README.md
!/architecture/
!/configs/
!/ui/
!/utilities/


# ─── n8n: one source file, everything else private ─────────────
# docker-compose.yml IS source - install-n8n.ps1 exits with
# "missing ...docker-compose.yml" without it, and never generates
# one. It holds no secrets: the encryption key is interpolated
# from n8n\.env at runtime, and .env stays ignored below.
#
# Everything else under n8n\ is private runtime data - workflows,
# credentials, the Postgres volume, agent memory.
!/n8n/
/n8n/*
!/n8n/docker-compose.yml


# ─── Junk inside those allowed folders ─────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Belt and braces.
#
#  Everything below is already excluded by the /* rule above.
#  It is repeated explicitly so that if anyone ever loosens the
#  allow-list, the private things stay private anyway.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# n8n — workflows, credentials, Postgres volume, Ollama blobs
# (no bare "n8n/" here: it would override the docker-compose.yml
#  exception above. /n8n/* already covers the directory.)
.n8n/
n8n-data/
workflows/
*[Ww][Oo][Rr][Kk][Ff][Ll][Oo][Ww]*.json
*[Cc][Rr][Ee][Dd][Ee][Nn][Tt][Ii][Aa][Ll]*.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
pgdata/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*_token*
*apikey*
*api_key*

# Weights, vendored runtimes, upstream checkout, logs
models/
tools/
repo/
logs/
.venv/
venv/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth

# Machine-specific state written by the installer
system.json

# Rollback state written by update-upstream.ps1 - records the commit this
# machine came from, which is meaningless on anyone else's.
/configs/.upstream-previous.json
